1
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,946
TAKE CHARGE OF MY HEART

2
00:00:31,489 --> 00:00:32,657
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

3
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:35,535
Yes?

4
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:37,662
Me too.

5
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:40,707
What do you mean?

6
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:42,959
When I'm

7
00:00:43,668 --> 00:00:45,795
with you,

8
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:48,757
I worry about you all the time.

9
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:50,800
My heart's racing so fast…

10
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,598
it feels like it will explode.

11
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:00,185
Ms. Na.

12
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:02,687
I…

13
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:08,276
don't want to die before my heart surgery.

14
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:11,446
Sorry?

15
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:12,947
So…

16
00:01:14,949 --> 00:01:19,245
just stay within
what I've planned and anticipated.

17
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:25,210
I'll go out first.

18
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:28,463
Don't let anyone see you come out.

19
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:36,012
Oh, right.

20
00:01:37,097 --> 00:01:39,724
Text me every 30 minutes
when you're with your friends.

21
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:43,895
Ugh, I feel dizzy.

22
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:05,750
Oh wow.

23
00:02:06,501 --> 00:02:09,254
I thought he was gonna confess
or something.

24
00:02:10,171 --> 00:02:12,841
Then again, there's no way
that jerk would do that.

25
00:02:16,803 --> 00:02:19,931
Our final concept
is "A Night's Confession."

26
00:02:20,014 --> 00:02:20,849
For this one,

27
00:02:20,932 --> 00:02:25,353
the story follows two longtime friends
who spend a night together at the resort.

28
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:30,024
Naturally, they end up confessing
their hidden feelings for each other.

29
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:31,484
That's all.

30
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:38,533
What do you think?

31
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:41,411
We put it together in script format,
like you suggested.

32
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:43,997
-Ms. Na, which do you like best?
-Me?

33
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:46,749
I think

34
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:50,587
the third concept
would be the easiest to dramatize.

35
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:53,506
How so?

36
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:56,092
The way they end up in the resort garden.

37
00:02:56,968 --> 00:02:59,596
Instead of following a past lover's trail,

38
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:01,431
what if we made it an adventure?

39
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:03,933
That could work.

40
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:08,188
Mr. Ji falls
into the mysterious world of TS Resort

41
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:10,356
and embarks on an adventure there.

42
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:13,943
As long as the protagonist's motivation
is clear from the start,

43
00:03:14,027 --> 00:03:16,154
viewers can immediately connect with them.

44
00:03:16,779 --> 00:03:18,740
The motivation doesn't have to be deep.

45
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:24,204
I think just a small sense of yearning
or a simple desire is enough

46
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:28,166
to carry the protagonist
through the story.

47
00:03:28,249 --> 00:03:31,669
And since it's only about a minute long…

48
00:03:37,550 --> 00:03:39,344
If we build a narrative like this,

49
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:41,387
it promotes TS Resort,

50
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:43,723
gives us a bit of drama,

51
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:47,518
and will be more fun
for Mr. Ji to act in… I think.

52
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:53,608
I like it. It sounds fun.

53
00:03:57,987 --> 00:04:00,031
You nailed the concept.
Let's give her a hand.

54
00:04:00,114 --> 00:04:01,574
That's it!

55
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:39,362
Door unlocked.

56
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:40,697
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

57
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:41,739
Yes?

58
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,491
Today…

59
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:49,539
You did well.

60
00:04:50,623 --> 00:04:53,835
Thanks to you,
we were able to finalize the concept.

61
00:04:54,585 --> 00:04:57,964
Before we leave for Jeju island,
I'm counting on you

62
00:04:59,465 --> 00:05:00,675
to write a great script.

63
00:05:02,927 --> 00:05:04,095
Jeez.

64
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:06,889
Did you think
my writing debut was a fluke?

65
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:09,142
A minute-long script?
I can do it in ten minutes.

66
00:05:09,225 --> 00:05:11,519
-You're getting carried away again.
-I'm not.

67
00:05:11,602 --> 00:05:14,105
Okay, maybe ten minutes is a stretch.

68
00:05:14,939 --> 00:05:18,359
Give me an hour,
and I'll write you a killer script.

69
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:19,360
You'll see.

70
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:22,989
Move over!

71
00:05:31,247 --> 00:05:32,957
Seriously…

72
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:48,306
Wow.

73
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:52,518
He thought something happened
to Na Bo-bae and rushed over.

74
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:54,354
Drove like he was racing.

75
00:05:55,104 --> 00:05:57,231
Freaking out, white as a ghost.

76
00:05:58,358 --> 00:06:01,778
Baek Ho-rang is serious about Na Bo-bae.

77
00:06:28,388 --> 00:06:29,222
Huh?

78
00:06:30,556 --> 00:06:31,641
What's wrong with me?

79
00:07:11,931 --> 00:07:12,765
Mr. Baek?

80
00:07:29,657 --> 00:07:31,325
Did you have something to say?

81
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:32,660
"Something to say"?

82
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:35,913
Do I look like
I have nothing better to do?

83
00:07:37,081 --> 00:07:38,207
Don't mind me.

84
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,377
Just do your job.

85
00:07:41,961 --> 00:07:43,337
What did I…

86
00:07:51,679 --> 00:07:52,889
Thank you.

87
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:55,516
Ms. Na.

88
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,518
I love the concept.

89
00:07:57,602 --> 00:07:58,436
Yes!

90
00:07:58,519 --> 00:08:01,898
Things he can experience
on his adventure at the resort…

91
00:08:02,398 --> 00:08:03,399
Sounds great.

92
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:25,087
Jeez, what's wrong with this?

93
00:08:29,091 --> 00:08:30,468
All right. Back to work.

94
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:33,554
Sir?

95
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:34,722
Sir!

96
00:08:36,307 --> 00:08:37,141
What was that?

97
00:08:38,434 --> 00:08:39,936
Did I do something wrong?

98
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:51,572
Is there something down there?

99
00:08:56,494 --> 00:08:57,662
The other day,

100
00:08:57,745 --> 00:08:59,830
Ms. Na and I were under the desk…

101
00:09:00,581 --> 00:09:02,083
What? When did you get here?

102
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:03,751
I've been here for a while.

103
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:08,339
Never mind.
Just spray some of that aroma spray.

104
00:09:10,299 --> 00:09:11,133
Yes, sir.

105
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:13,052
By the way, sir.

106
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:17,682
You seem to be getting
a little too involved with Ms. Na.

107
00:09:18,182 --> 00:09:19,850
I suggest you keep your distance.

108
00:09:21,143 --> 00:09:23,604
Should I just send everyone on vacation?

109
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:24,522
Sorry?

110
00:09:24,605 --> 00:09:27,275
I could send everyone on vacation
and charge at home…

111
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:31,696
I mean…

112
00:09:32,738 --> 00:09:36,117
It'd be nice
to take some time to recharge.

113
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,868
That's what I meant.

114
00:09:37,952 --> 00:09:38,786
Sir.

115
00:09:39,495 --> 00:09:42,206
We have a business trip to Jeju tomorrow.

116
00:09:44,375 --> 00:09:45,585
Ms. Na just texted.

117
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:48,004
Did you hear me?

118
00:09:48,087 --> 00:09:50,298
Why did she text me out of the blue?

119
00:09:50,381 --> 00:09:52,967
Mr. Baek Ho-rang!
I'm heading out first today.

120
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:55,803
It's my sister's birthday,
so I'm throwing her a party.

121
00:09:55,886 --> 00:09:57,471
I'll come home tonight.

122
00:10:04,353 --> 00:10:05,396
Damn it.

123
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:07,940
Sir!

124
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:11,527
Sir!

125
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:12,486
Well…

126
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:14,739
Did Ms. Na already leave?

127
00:10:14,822 --> 00:10:17,450
Yes, she said she had plans
and left right away.

128
00:10:17,533 --> 00:10:19,327
Did you need her for something?

129
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:20,786
What? No.

130
00:10:21,787 --> 00:10:24,081
Call it a day.
See you at the airport tomorrow.

131
00:10:24,165 --> 00:10:25,082
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

132
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:26,167
Take care, sir.

133
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:27,293
See you tomorrow.

134
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:34,383
Sir.

135
00:10:35,926 --> 00:10:37,094
Hey.

136
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:41,390
Our little sister is here!

137
00:10:41,932 --> 00:10:43,684
HAPPY BIRTHDAY!

138
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:47,271
Why does he always make such a fuss?

139
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:49,607
You hungry?
What should we order for dinner?

140
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:51,484
Order whatever you want.

141
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:53,694
I got us lots of beer!

142
00:10:53,778 --> 00:10:55,279
Ta-da!

143
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:57,948
It's Ji-hye's birthday.
She should get to choose.

144
00:10:58,032 --> 00:10:58,866
That's right.

145
00:10:58,949 --> 00:10:59,950
It's my birthday,

146
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:02,953
so the writer with the new Gangnam studio
should treat us.

147
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:06,499
Of course! What do you want to eat?

148
00:11:06,582 --> 00:11:08,209
-What should we order?
-Chicken!

149
00:11:08,292 --> 00:11:10,211
-Fried chicken!
-Chicken?

150
00:11:39,031 --> 00:11:41,450
I'm so full.

151
00:11:42,118 --> 00:11:42,952
Na Bo-bae!

152
00:11:43,035 --> 00:11:45,788
It sure is nice
to have a successful little sister.

153
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:47,415
Successful? Please.

154
00:11:47,998 --> 00:11:49,417
My show isn't even out yet.

155
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:51,335
When your show's out,

156
00:11:51,419 --> 00:11:53,587
fried chicken and tteokbokki won't cut it.

157
00:11:53,671 --> 00:11:55,131
We'll have to get
some premium Korean beef.

158
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:56,882
Your show…

159
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:58,801
When's it coming out?

160
00:12:00,219 --> 00:12:02,221
Well, I'm not sure.

161
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:06,434
Shows take at least a few years
to come out,

162
00:12:06,517 --> 00:12:09,019
so it'll probably be a while.

163
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:12,940
We've already waited three years.
Now we have to wait even longer?

164
00:12:13,023 --> 00:12:15,025
Well, maybe another year…

165
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:16,485
Or two?

166
00:12:20,614 --> 00:12:22,283
Something's fishy.

167
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:24,869
Is it really going well?

168
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:28,539
Of course!

169
00:12:28,622 --> 00:12:33,002
I've been doing a ton of research,
and my script's coming along well.

170
00:12:33,085 --> 00:12:35,504
My romance scenes
are so much better now. And…

171
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:39,008
When I'm

172
00:12:39,508 --> 00:12:41,969
with you,

173
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:45,347
I worry about you every day.

174
00:12:46,056 --> 00:12:47,558
My heart's racing so fast…

175
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:50,436
it feels like it will explode.

176
00:12:52,563 --> 00:12:53,814
And what?

177
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:56,358
What were you thinking about?
You totally spaced out.

178
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:57,568
Huh?

179
00:12:57,651 --> 00:12:58,819
What?

180
00:12:58,903 --> 00:13:00,780
-What? I did not.
-Huh?

181
00:13:00,863 --> 00:13:03,324
She's acting really weird.
What's going on?

182
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:04,909
I know, right?

183
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:08,370
That's the look

184
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:12,374
Na Ji-hye gets
when she thinks about her fiancé.

185
00:13:12,458 --> 00:13:14,126
What are you talking about?

186
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:15,711
Fiancé?

187
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:19,715
You two are hilarious.

188
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:22,802
How could you say that
when I've been working so hard?

189
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:28,057
Ji-hye,
something's definitely up with her.

190
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:29,558
I can feel it.

191
00:13:33,604 --> 00:13:35,064
You seeing someone?

192
00:13:35,147 --> 00:13:37,274
Seeing someone? I have to write my script!

193
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:38,609
Also…

194
00:13:39,652 --> 00:13:42,279
Did you forget about my electric powers?

195
00:13:42,363 --> 00:13:43,447
I'm leaving.

196
00:13:43,531 --> 00:13:45,324
-Huh?
-Where do you think you're going?

197
00:13:48,285 --> 00:13:49,495
You should stay the night.

198
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:53,541
You're acting really suspicious.
Trying to run away?

199
00:13:53,624 --> 00:13:56,043
Where are you going?
Don't make me use tae kwon do on you!

200
00:13:56,126 --> 00:13:59,004
I… Then I'll use my electric powers!

201
00:14:15,187 --> 00:14:17,231
When is she coming home?

202
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:24,697
PORTABLE CHARGER

203
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:28,158
Hello?

204
00:14:29,076 --> 00:14:32,913
Oh, Mr. Baek. I'm sorry,
I don't think I can come home today.

205
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:35,332
Why not? You said you'd be back tonight.

206
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:38,377
My sister and brother
insist that I stay the night.

207
00:14:38,961 --> 00:14:41,964
I said I have a work trip tomorrow,
but they said I should leave from here

208
00:14:42,047 --> 00:14:44,341
since it's closer to the airport
and I have all my stuff.

209
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:46,594
What do we do about charging you?

210
00:14:46,677 --> 00:14:48,679
Should I sneak out at dawn?

211
00:14:50,222 --> 00:14:54,184
I've got enough charge to last
about 20 hours, even if we're apart.

212
00:14:54,935 --> 00:14:57,605
You can supercharge me
at the airport tomorrow.

213
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:00,691
Don't worry. Stay the night.

214
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:01,859
But still--

215
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:03,402
I said it's fine.

216
00:15:03,485 --> 00:15:05,237
You'll be busy tomorrow.

217
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:08,282
Take this opportunity
to relax with your family.

218
00:15:08,782 --> 00:15:11,035
Thank you. See you tomorrow.

219
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:31,680
What's wrong with me?

220
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:34,600
Baek Ho-rang, are you crazy?

221
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:51,408
Oh!

222
00:15:51,909 --> 00:15:54,286
I said I'd redecorate the garage for her.

223
00:15:55,704 --> 00:15:56,538
That's right.

224
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,958
That's why I kept thinking about her.

225
00:15:59,041 --> 00:16:00,376
So that's what it was.

226
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:05,965
Hey, Mr. Yoon. It's me.

227
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:08,634
Find me an interior designer.
The best one.

228
00:16:08,717 --> 00:16:10,094
Sir? Right now?

229
00:16:10,177 --> 00:16:11,428
Yeah, right now.

230
00:16:12,012 --> 00:16:14,723
-Mr. Yoon, ever heard of flexing?
-Sorry?

231
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:17,768
I want a top-of-the-line interior.
A real chaebol flex.

232
00:16:17,851 --> 00:16:18,727
Got it?

233
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:21,438
I don't know what has you so worried
at this hour, but--

234
00:16:21,522 --> 00:16:23,065
No, listen.

235
00:16:23,148 --> 00:16:24,400
I really need it.

236
00:16:24,483 --> 00:16:26,735
And send over a cake

237
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:30,155
and the finest Korean beef right now.

238
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:31,532
Yeah.

239
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:44,044
Will his battery really last the night?

240
00:16:45,796 --> 00:16:47,339
RUBBER GLOVE

241
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:49,883
MR. BAEK HO-R

242
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:51,802
Never mind.

243
00:16:52,302 --> 00:16:53,470
Forget it.

244
00:16:58,892 --> 00:17:00,978
JOSEE, THE TIGER AND THE FISH

245
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:08,277
HO-RANG

246
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:11,905
Why can't I focus?

247
00:17:12,489 --> 00:17:14,241
Come on. Focus.

248
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:23,959
I-HYEOK AND HYE-JU
WALK THROUGH THE HAUNTED HOUSE

249
00:17:24,043 --> 00:17:25,252
I'm a little scared.

250
00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:26,628
(FEARFULLY)

251
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:28,213
Can we just get out of here?

252
00:17:30,257 --> 00:17:31,258
Ma'am.

253
00:17:31,341 --> 00:17:32,176
(FINDING HER CUTE)

254
00:17:32,259 --> 00:17:33,635
I didn't expect you to be this scared.

255
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:35,471
You're not scared?

256
00:17:35,554 --> 00:17:36,555
(DEFENSIVELY)

257
00:17:36,638 --> 00:17:38,307
I hate jump scares and--

258
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:40,684
(THROWING HERSELF INTO HIS ARMS)

259
00:17:43,145 --> 00:17:44,563
I'm scared.

260
00:17:48,901 --> 00:17:50,569
I-HYEOK HOLDS HYE-JU'S HAND

261
00:17:50,652 --> 00:17:52,029
Ma'am.

262
00:17:52,112 --> 00:17:53,322
Run.

263
00:17:56,241 --> 00:17:58,869
I-HYEOK RUNS, HOLDING HYE-JU'S HAND TIGHT

264
00:18:01,914 --> 00:18:05,417
NOTHING SCARES HYE-JU AND I-HYEOK ANYMORE

265
00:18:15,135 --> 00:18:16,095
That's more like it.

266
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:19,056
Yeah, the male lead should be holding
the female lead's hand.

267
00:18:19,139 --> 00:18:22,810
Running with the ghost? Makes no sense.

268
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:27,815
Baek Ho-rang. He's hilarious.

269
00:18:32,694 --> 00:18:36,657
That's the look Na Ji-hye gets
when she thinks about her fiancé.

270
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:37,658
You seeing someone?

271
00:18:38,659 --> 00:18:40,452
Hilarious? Not at all.

272
00:18:41,036 --> 00:18:42,663
Seeing someone? Yeah, right.

273
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:45,874
It's an act of compassion.

274
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:47,084
I'm saving a life.

275
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:49,419
Besides, Mr. Baek has Ms. Han.

276
00:18:54,591 --> 00:18:57,386
And since it's an act of compassion,

277
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:04,977
it should be okay to call
and ask how much battery he has left.

278
00:19:08,605 --> 00:19:09,606
No!

279
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:11,441
No.

280
00:19:12,151 --> 00:19:13,110
No.

281
00:19:13,610 --> 00:19:15,320
Get a grip.

282
00:19:30,502 --> 00:19:32,671
Mr. Baek, what are you doing here?

283
00:19:33,547 --> 00:19:36,258
Well, I…

284
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:37,759
It's your sister's birthday.

285
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:40,179
I thought it'd be rude
to not acknowledge it,

286
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:44,641
since you help charge my battery and all.

287
00:19:45,392 --> 00:19:46,393
And I realized

288
00:19:47,019 --> 00:19:49,980
you wished me a happy birthday too, so…

289
00:19:51,231 --> 00:19:52,107
But…

290
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:56,820
So you bought all that
and ran all the way here at this hour?

291
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:58,655
I didn't run. I drove here.

292
00:19:58,739 --> 00:20:01,074
And Mr. Yoon bought these.

293
00:20:01,575 --> 00:20:02,743
Don't get the wrong idea.

294
00:20:02,826 --> 00:20:06,580
TS Resort
takes employee welfare seriously.

295
00:20:06,663 --> 00:20:07,664
But…

296
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:10,459
Employee welfare? At this hour?

297
00:20:10,542 --> 00:20:11,877
Take it. Come on.

298
00:20:16,423 --> 00:20:19,509
What? You're just leaving?
What about your charge?

299
00:20:20,093 --> 00:20:21,220
Huh? Charge?

300
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:25,098
Well, I'm at 85% now.

301
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:27,601
If I lose 4% an hour,

302
00:20:27,684 --> 00:20:30,979
I'll still have 50% if we meet by 6 a.m.

303
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,565
So there's no need to worry.

304
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:34,983
But still--

305
00:20:35,067 --> 00:20:37,361
And I'm not that weak.

306
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:52,793
Close the window before bed.
See you tomorrow.

307
00:20:52,876 --> 00:20:54,378
But Mr. Baek…

308
00:20:58,131 --> 00:20:59,174
What…

309
00:21:27,619 --> 00:21:30,831
It's bad for my heart if it gets too high.

310
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:33,625
Calm down.

311
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:49,057
Stop it.

312
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:29,598
Was he thinking about me

313
00:22:30,515 --> 00:22:31,516
the whole time?

314
00:22:38,357 --> 00:22:39,316
What am I saying?

315
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:41,276
Get a grip, Na Bo-bae.

316
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:42,778
Get a grip.

317
00:23:03,131 --> 00:23:04,383
Ms. Na Bo-bae!

318
00:23:05,384 --> 00:23:06,760
Mr. Baek Ho-rang!

319
00:23:22,109 --> 00:23:23,652
Oh, to be young again.

320
00:23:23,735 --> 00:23:26,863
Looks like one of them's been abroad
for a few years.

321
00:23:33,453 --> 00:23:35,330
I need a charge.

322
00:23:35,414 --> 00:23:36,665
Yeah.

323
00:23:36,748 --> 00:23:39,292
I was up all night working.

324
00:23:39,376 --> 00:23:42,337
That must be why
my battery's draining faster than usual.

325
00:23:43,463 --> 00:23:46,049
-I'm worried about my heart.
-So you were up all night.

326
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:46,967
Yes.

327
00:23:47,050 --> 00:23:48,802
I rushed over because of your battery.

328
00:23:48,885 --> 00:23:51,346
Really, that was the only reason.

329
00:23:52,681 --> 00:23:53,807
Thank you

330
00:23:53,890 --> 00:23:56,309
for caring about my life.

331
00:23:56,393 --> 00:23:58,687
It's just an act of compassion.

332
00:23:58,770 --> 00:24:00,439
Oh, an act of compassion?

333
00:24:04,943 --> 00:24:06,945
Supercharging here is too risky.

334
00:24:07,028 --> 00:24:08,655
Let's go to the VIP lounge.

335
00:24:09,239 --> 00:24:10,282
Let's go. Quickly.

336
00:24:18,123 --> 00:24:19,416
Mr. Baek.

337
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:21,001
You're early.

338
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:22,961
Oh, yes.

339
00:24:24,629 --> 00:24:25,464
Yes.

340
00:24:26,715 --> 00:24:28,925
You're here early too, Ms. Han.

341
00:24:29,593 --> 00:24:31,511
Three hours early.

342
00:24:32,262 --> 00:24:35,307
I figured you'd get here
three or four hours early.

343
00:24:37,767 --> 00:24:38,602
Have a seat.

344
00:24:39,102 --> 00:24:40,812
Let's grab a quick breakfast.

345
00:24:42,939 --> 00:24:44,608
Sure. Let's do that.

346
00:24:45,609 --> 00:24:46,985
Hold on.

347
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:51,615
I have to get something from Mr. Yoon.

348
00:24:51,698 --> 00:24:52,532
Excuse me.

349
00:24:54,075 --> 00:24:54,951
Sure. Go ahead.

350
00:24:55,785 --> 00:24:56,620
All right.

351
00:25:07,881 --> 00:25:09,925
I don't think we can do it in the lounge.

352
00:25:10,634 --> 00:25:13,011
Let's just do it here. Nobody's around.

353
00:25:13,094 --> 00:25:14,888
First, put your sunglasses on.

354
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:22,521
No, I'm serious.

355
00:25:24,481 --> 00:25:25,815
-No. Not this way.
-Shoot.

356
00:25:26,316 --> 00:25:27,150
Wait up!

357
00:25:27,234 --> 00:25:29,986
You know you have to take off your shoes
on the plane, right?

358
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:31,404
Seriously, Ms. Yang?

359
00:25:31,488 --> 00:25:33,615
Even schoolkids
don't fall for that anymore.

360
00:25:33,698 --> 00:25:34,866
But it's true.

361
00:25:35,617 --> 00:25:37,285
Are we going on vacation?

362
00:25:37,369 --> 00:25:39,412
What's with the outfit, Mr. Lee?

363
00:25:39,496 --> 00:25:42,332
I dressed up a little.
I'll change when we get there.

364
00:25:42,415 --> 00:25:43,291
Seriously.

365
00:25:43,375 --> 00:25:45,752
Ms. Na said she'd come separately.

366
00:25:45,835 --> 00:25:46,795
Isn't she here yet?

367
00:25:46,878 --> 00:25:49,839
Why would she come separately?
She's probably with Mr. Baek.

368
00:25:54,594 --> 00:25:57,138
Damn it, they keep popping up.
What do we do?

369
00:25:57,222 --> 00:25:59,766
At this rate, I can't charge you.
What's your battery at?

370
00:26:01,476 --> 00:26:03,687
Right now, it's at 35%.

371
00:26:03,770 --> 00:26:04,813
Thirty-five?

372
00:26:08,775 --> 00:26:09,776
Follow me.

373
00:26:13,863 --> 00:26:16,241
You're eating breakfast
at a time like this?

374
00:26:16,324 --> 00:26:19,119
No one from the company will come here.

375
00:26:19,202 --> 00:26:21,955
It's a good hiding spot.
Staying close won't look suspicious.

376
00:26:22,038 --> 00:26:23,665
Don't sit there. Sit next to me.

377
00:26:23,748 --> 00:26:24,624
Oh.

378
00:26:35,552 --> 00:26:38,888
Your jeyuk and doenjang-jjigae.

379
00:26:38,972 --> 00:26:40,307
Enjoy your meal.

380
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:42,017
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

381
00:26:46,021 --> 00:26:47,063
Let's…

382
00:26:47,147 --> 00:26:49,149
Let's eat while we…

383
00:26:49,232 --> 00:26:50,400
-Just come.
-Sure.

384
00:26:50,483 --> 00:26:52,527
-You talk too much.
-Your luggage…

385
00:26:52,611 --> 00:26:54,321
-Wait, Director.
-Stop whining.

386
00:26:54,404 --> 00:26:55,739
Just come.

387
00:26:55,822 --> 00:26:57,741
-Follow me.
-Why do you have so much luggage?

388
00:26:57,824 --> 00:26:59,993
-Be careful with them.
-They're heavy.

389
00:27:00,076 --> 00:27:02,871
You gotta hit a Korean restaurant
at the airport.

390
00:27:03,663 --> 00:27:06,708
Why eat Korean food
when we're going to Jeju?

391
00:27:06,791 --> 00:27:09,502
It's just my little pre-flight ritual.

392
00:27:09,586 --> 00:27:11,588
Just eat. Enough complaining.

393
00:27:20,430 --> 00:27:21,765
Huh?

394
00:27:22,891 --> 00:27:24,267
-What's that?
-What?

395
00:27:26,353 --> 00:27:27,437
Say what?

396
00:27:33,568 --> 00:27:35,528
What are they eating? It must be good.

397
00:27:35,612 --> 00:27:37,072
Their faces are buried in the bowl.

398
00:27:37,155 --> 00:27:38,073
-Seo-jeong.
-Yes?

399
00:27:38,156 --> 00:27:39,032
Let's have that.

400
00:27:39,115 --> 00:27:40,116
Sure.

401
00:27:40,200 --> 00:27:41,951
They could've sat across from each other.

402
00:27:42,035 --> 00:27:44,913
Couples can be so over the top, you know.

403
00:27:45,622 --> 00:27:46,498
So over the top.

404
00:27:46,998 --> 00:27:48,041
I'm divorced, you know.

405
00:27:49,417 --> 00:27:51,753
Okay, I'll go order.
The company card, please.

406
00:27:52,337 --> 00:27:54,047
Can't you just go?

407
00:27:54,130 --> 00:27:56,299
-Company card!
-I don't have it. You pay.

408
00:27:56,383 --> 00:27:59,094
-We'll split it.
-Split it? I'll split your head open.

409
00:27:59,969 --> 00:28:01,763
-You want everything free.
-What's that?

410
00:28:01,846 --> 00:28:03,640
Doenjang-jjigae. Bibimbap.

411
00:28:04,140 --> 00:28:06,059
-Where do I order Korean food?
-Chopsticks…

412
00:28:06,559 --> 00:28:07,519
Where are they?

413
00:28:18,738 --> 00:28:21,282
Excuse me.
Where are the chopsticks and spoons?

414
00:28:23,576 --> 00:28:25,286
What's your battery at now?

415
00:28:25,370 --> 00:28:26,663
It's at 41%.

416
00:28:26,746 --> 00:28:28,373
It's still risky.

417
00:28:31,584 --> 00:28:35,046
I think we should finish charging
on the plane.

418
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:53,481
Mr. Yoon. Ms. Na Bo-bae…

419
00:28:54,149 --> 00:28:56,317
I mean, the secretaries. Where are they?

420
00:28:56,401 --> 00:28:59,904
I think there was a mix-up
with the reservation.

421
00:28:59,988 --> 00:29:03,116
The other secretaries and staff
are in economy.

422
00:29:03,992 --> 00:29:06,661
Oh. Economy?

423
00:29:06,745 --> 00:29:10,540
Economy's over ten meters away.

424
00:29:28,641 --> 00:29:31,770
What took so long?
We said we'd meet after the seatbelt sign.

425
00:29:31,853 --> 00:29:33,271
I've got too many eyes on me.

426
00:29:34,731 --> 00:29:37,150
Let's hug and get it over with
before anyone comes.

427
00:29:38,026 --> 00:29:39,652
Is the passenger check complete?

428
00:29:39,736 --> 00:29:40,945
-Yes, it's done.
-What the…

429
00:29:41,029 --> 00:29:43,281
-Let's get the drink cart ready.
-Okay.

430
00:29:53,625 --> 00:29:56,085
I'll get the cups. You get the drinks.

431
00:29:56,169 --> 00:29:57,170
Sure.

432
00:29:59,798 --> 00:30:03,676
Please prepare the sodas and other drinks.
And the coffee too.

433
00:30:24,864 --> 00:30:27,325
What is it? Did we land?

434
00:30:29,786 --> 00:30:31,746
Please fasten your seat belt.

435
00:30:33,873 --> 00:30:35,750
Seat belt. Ms. Go, your seat belt.

436
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:38,211
-Please fasten your seat belt.
-What? Are we there?

437
00:30:39,337 --> 00:30:41,548
Please be seated
and fasten your seat belt.

438
00:30:41,631 --> 00:30:42,882
What happened?

439
00:30:43,466 --> 00:30:45,176
-I'm sorry.
-Don't do that!

440
00:30:45,260 --> 00:30:46,845
The plane shook again.

441
00:30:59,315 --> 00:31:02,402
I'm sorry. I thought I was going to fall.

442
00:31:02,485 --> 00:31:03,862
Did I startle you?

443
00:31:03,945 --> 00:31:06,614
No. Not at all.

444
00:31:07,615 --> 00:31:09,701
It's the turbulence.

445
00:31:09,784 --> 00:31:13,246
This airline has an A safety rating
for domestic flights.

446
00:31:13,329 --> 00:31:15,748
Very low accident rate.
That's why I chose it.

447
00:31:15,832 --> 00:31:17,333
Why's this thing beeping?

448
00:31:17,417 --> 00:31:19,669
You weren't startled,
so why's your heart rate…

449
00:31:21,546 --> 00:31:22,422
Could it be…

450
00:31:22,505 --> 00:31:23,882
I was just startled!

451
00:31:23,965 --> 00:31:25,341
Don't get the wrong idea.

452
00:31:26,384 --> 00:31:27,468
I was just startled.

453
00:31:27,552 --> 00:31:29,095
I didn't say anything.

454
00:31:30,555 --> 00:31:31,848
Are you all right?

455
00:31:32,348 --> 00:31:34,350
We're experiencing turbulence.

456
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:37,562
Please return to your seat
until it subsides.

457
00:31:39,188 --> 00:31:41,149
My stomach's acting up.

458
00:31:41,232 --> 00:31:43,818
I'm kind of in the middle of it.
I can't really stop.

459
00:31:44,611 --> 00:31:46,571
I'll just stay seated here.

460
00:31:48,364 --> 00:31:50,074
All right.

461
00:31:56,414 --> 00:31:57,498
Ms. Na.

462
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:00,168
You can't stop?

463
00:32:00,251 --> 00:32:03,254
Oh, be quiet.

464
00:32:07,634 --> 00:32:09,928
We'll charge again later
if we get a chance.

465
00:32:10,595 --> 00:32:12,847
I think it's okay now,
so I'll head out first.

466
00:32:12,931 --> 00:32:14,223
Come out in a bit.

467
00:32:15,934 --> 00:32:18,061
Stop laughing!

468
00:32:35,370 --> 00:32:37,121
It's so hot in here.

469
00:32:48,341 --> 00:32:50,343
-Nice, right?
-Yes, very.

470
00:32:58,518 --> 00:32:59,936
It's been a while, Mr. Heo.

471
00:33:00,019 --> 00:33:02,355
It's an honor
to have you here in Jeju, sir.

472
00:33:02,438 --> 00:33:04,065
The honor's all mine.

473
00:33:04,148 --> 00:33:06,150
You run this place so well.

474
00:33:06,234 --> 00:33:08,486
Our Seoul resort has a lot to live up to.

475
00:33:08,569 --> 00:33:10,029
Not at all.

476
00:33:10,113 --> 00:33:11,739
The filming locations are all set,

477
00:33:11,823 --> 00:33:14,200
and the actor's already here.

478
00:33:14,283 --> 00:33:15,576
-Is that so?
-Yes.

479
00:33:18,579 --> 00:33:20,498
-Hello.
-Hello.

480
00:33:21,582 --> 00:33:22,625
Hello.

481
00:33:23,668 --> 00:33:25,837
-Looking good as always.
-You're too kind.

482
00:33:29,590 --> 00:33:30,466
Have you eaten?

483
00:33:30,550 --> 00:33:32,176
Yeah. You?

484
00:33:37,557 --> 00:33:41,102
I heard you weren't arriving
until this afternoon.

485
00:33:41,602 --> 00:33:45,815
I wanted to check out the set,
so I shuffled my schedule and came early.

486
00:33:49,777 --> 00:33:52,447
Awesome! This room's really nice too.

487
00:33:52,947 --> 00:33:55,533
This is insane. The view's incredible.

488
00:33:57,452 --> 00:33:59,412
I need a photo of this.

489
00:34:00,747 --> 00:34:04,167
Wow, I think the rooms here
are better than ours.

490
00:34:05,877 --> 00:34:08,546
Ms. Go, which room are you staying in?

491
00:34:08,629 --> 00:34:09,630
Let me see.

492
00:34:10,798 --> 00:34:12,008
Wow.

493
00:34:15,762 --> 00:34:16,846
Ms. Na.

494
00:34:19,640 --> 00:34:20,475
Yes?

495
00:34:23,853 --> 00:34:25,605
Mr. Baek is asking for you.

496
00:34:43,581 --> 00:34:45,666
Mr. Yoon, why are you here?

497
00:34:47,502 --> 00:34:49,545
Am I not allowed to be here?

498
00:34:50,129 --> 00:34:53,091
You're just charging.

499
00:34:58,429 --> 00:35:00,098
No. Get out.

500
00:35:02,141 --> 00:35:03,017
Huh?

501
00:35:03,101 --> 00:35:04,435
Get out.

502
00:35:06,437 --> 00:35:07,522
Huh?

503
00:35:07,605 --> 00:35:08,564
You're not leaving?

504
00:35:10,108 --> 00:35:11,317
Well…

505
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:13,528
I mean, wouldn't it be okay

506
00:35:14,028 --> 00:35:15,196
for him to stay?

507
00:35:15,279 --> 00:35:17,073
We're just charging. No big deal.

508
00:35:17,156 --> 00:35:18,741
You said it's an act of compassion.

509
00:35:18,825 --> 00:35:22,120
If we're charging
in the name of such a noble cause,

510
00:35:22,620 --> 00:35:25,081
shouldn't we keep it private and sacred?

511
00:35:27,208 --> 00:35:28,251
But…

512
00:35:28,334 --> 00:35:31,379
-I mean, he already knows everything--
-I'm very sensitive.

513
00:35:31,462 --> 00:35:33,798
I get distracted
when there's someone around.

514
00:35:35,842 --> 00:35:37,093
Get out.

515
00:35:38,136 --> 00:35:39,887
I told you to get out.

516
00:35:39,971 --> 00:35:41,848
Go keep a lookout or something!

517
00:35:42,473 --> 00:35:44,892
Are you doing something
that needs a lookout?

518
00:35:59,782 --> 00:36:02,076
I could've finished charging by now.
Get out now.

519
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:03,494
You're not leaving?

520
00:36:04,245 --> 00:36:05,204
Get out already.

521
00:36:09,292 --> 00:36:10,668
Get out!

522
00:36:20,928 --> 00:36:22,763
TS HOTEL VICE PRESIDENT YOON DONG-SEOK

523
00:36:30,021 --> 00:36:30,855
Yes.

524
00:36:33,399 --> 00:36:34,400
It's me.

525
00:36:42,533 --> 00:36:44,410
He just won't listen.

526
00:36:49,832 --> 00:36:51,876
Shall we… do it now?

527
00:36:54,086 --> 00:36:54,921
I guess.

528
00:36:55,004 --> 00:36:56,088
Well…

529
00:36:57,840 --> 00:36:58,674
Here.

530
00:37:11,938 --> 00:37:13,314
Oh, it's over 50%.

531
00:37:13,397 --> 00:37:15,691
It's half full.
That's in the safe range, isn't it?

532
00:37:16,943 --> 00:37:17,777
Actually…

533
00:37:21,030 --> 00:37:22,240
Ms. Na Bo-bae?

534
00:37:23,241 --> 00:37:24,242
Yes?

535
00:37:24,825 --> 00:37:25,660
I was

536
00:37:26,160 --> 00:37:28,996
just talking about holding hands.

537
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:34,919
What? Oh gosh.

538
00:37:37,380 --> 00:37:38,673
I thought…

539
00:37:38,756 --> 00:37:42,510
You opened your arms wide like this,
so I thought you wanted a hug.

540
00:37:42,593 --> 00:37:43,511
That's why I…

541
00:37:43,594 --> 00:37:46,472
Man, this is more than enough.

542
00:37:46,555 --> 00:37:48,140
-Thank you.
-Sure.

543
00:37:48,224 --> 00:37:49,225
Yeah.

544
00:37:50,476 --> 00:37:51,727
Then I'll…

545
00:37:52,353 --> 00:37:53,604
Who was it?

546
00:37:53,688 --> 00:37:56,899
Oh, the director. I'll go over
the script one last time with him.

547
00:37:56,983 --> 00:37:58,067
Okay.

548
00:37:59,777 --> 00:38:01,070
-I'll get going.
-See you.

549
00:38:04,156 --> 00:38:05,658
Thank you.

550
00:38:05,741 --> 00:38:07,618
Oh. Sure.

551
00:38:26,137 --> 00:38:27,972
-The butterfly…
-Stop asking me.

552
00:38:28,055 --> 00:38:29,223
Sorry I'm late.

553
00:38:29,307 --> 00:38:30,975
Go to the set already!

554
00:38:31,058 --> 00:38:33,185
-We'll go without the butterfly.
-Ms. Na.

555
00:38:33,269 --> 00:38:34,562
How do we express this?

556
00:38:34,645 --> 00:38:36,022
Where? Oh, here.

557
00:38:36,731 --> 00:38:38,607
-Is it done?
-Looks like an early wrap.

558
00:38:38,691 --> 00:38:40,568
-Can I see the script?
-Here.

559
00:38:46,365 --> 00:38:48,868
Ms. Na, I have a question.

560
00:38:49,869 --> 00:38:50,703
Yeah.

561
00:38:50,786 --> 00:38:52,455
-The emotion here…
-Which part?

562
00:38:52,538 --> 00:38:54,248
I just wanted an excuse to talk.

563
00:38:55,249 --> 00:38:56,500
The script's great.

564
00:38:56,584 --> 00:38:58,002
Oh, come on.

565
00:38:58,544 --> 00:39:01,630
It's only one minute long,
but your hard work shows.

566
00:39:01,714 --> 00:39:05,009
It's in script format,
but it's my first commercial.

567
00:39:05,092 --> 00:39:06,010
Is it okay?

568
00:39:07,428 --> 00:39:09,138
What's with those two?

569
00:39:09,847 --> 00:39:11,557
So you noticed it too.

570
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:12,475
Yeah.

571
00:39:12,558 --> 00:39:16,228
Do you think something's going on
between those two?

572
00:39:17,271 --> 00:39:20,232
I thought Ms. Na and Mr. Baek
were a sure thing,

573
00:39:20,316 --> 00:39:22,109
but maybe it's those two instead.

574
00:39:22,193 --> 00:39:24,695
Come on. Watch what you say.

575
00:39:25,196 --> 00:39:26,614
You said it too, Ms. Go.

576
00:39:26,697 --> 00:39:27,656
Well…

577
00:39:28,157 --> 00:39:31,869
I mean, they look good together.

578
00:39:39,835 --> 00:39:42,546
Look good together? Give me a break.

579
00:39:56,352 --> 00:39:58,479
Shouldn't he go deeper?

580
00:39:58,562 --> 00:39:59,688
Looks good to me.

581
00:39:59,772 --> 00:40:01,690
Besides, it's really shallow here.

582
00:40:01,774 --> 00:40:02,900
No.

583
00:40:03,526 --> 00:40:07,363
I think he should dive from here to here
and do a few laps

584
00:40:07,446 --> 00:40:09,448
to make it look real.

585
00:40:09,532 --> 00:40:10,866
Is that really necessary?

586
00:40:11,742 --> 00:40:14,745
Aren't you a professional?
Isn't directing all about the visuals?

587
00:40:14,829 --> 00:40:18,874
He should dive, swim around,
and spin like a dolphin

588
00:40:18,958 --> 00:40:24,380
so we can really show off
how big the pool is at TS Resort Jeju.

589
00:40:24,463 --> 00:40:25,840
Not even pro swimmers would do that.

590
00:40:25,923 --> 00:40:27,174
Excuse me?

591
00:40:27,258 --> 00:40:29,218
Okay, fine.

592
00:40:29,301 --> 00:40:30,469
Cut.

593
00:40:30,970 --> 00:40:33,389
Sorry, but let's shoot that again.

594
00:40:33,472 --> 00:40:35,516
Eun-ho, sorry, but after a short break,

595
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:38,978
could you swim butterfly like a dolphin
from here to there?

596
00:40:39,061 --> 00:40:39,979
Sure.

597
00:40:42,940 --> 00:40:45,276
Tell him to do three laps.

598
00:40:45,776 --> 00:40:47,570
We may have to do it a few times.

599
00:40:47,653 --> 00:40:48,571
Sure.

600
00:40:48,654 --> 00:40:49,697
Sorry. Thank you.

601
00:40:50,197 --> 00:40:51,490
Happy now?

602
00:40:53,242 --> 00:40:55,327
-Ms. Na.
-Yes.

603
00:40:57,079 --> 00:40:58,122
Well…

604
00:40:58,205 --> 00:40:59,415
How did I do?

605
00:41:00,040 --> 00:41:01,375
I should've worked out more.

606
00:41:04,170 --> 00:41:06,714
No. You already look great.

607
00:41:10,968 --> 00:41:14,472
Did she just give Ji Eun-ho's abs
a thumbs-up?

608
00:41:16,932 --> 00:41:19,351
I'm nervous because you're watching me.

609
00:41:19,435 --> 00:41:20,936
I might be shaking a little.

610
00:41:21,562 --> 00:41:24,440
I told you not to go around
flirting without thinking.

611
00:41:24,523 --> 00:41:26,942
What do you mean, without thinking?
I mean it.

612
00:41:33,866 --> 00:41:36,076
See? People get the wrong idea.

613
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:38,287
No. They won't.

614
00:41:39,038 --> 00:41:40,831
-Aren't you cold?
-I'm fine.

615
00:41:43,167 --> 00:41:44,793
Do you want some water?

616
00:41:45,836 --> 00:41:46,670
What's…

617
00:41:49,173 --> 00:41:50,508
Go take a break.

618
00:41:51,133 --> 00:41:52,176
What's with him?

619
00:42:02,019 --> 00:42:04,271
-We'll start with the dolphin!
-Yeah.

620
00:42:04,355 --> 00:42:05,231
Eun-ho, you okay?

621
00:42:05,314 --> 00:42:06,690
-Let's go!
-I think it's great.

622
00:42:06,774 --> 00:42:08,901
-I love it.
-I know.

623
00:42:09,818 --> 00:42:10,778
Thanks.

624
00:42:22,623 --> 00:42:25,209
Eun-ho! Why are you at the grill?

625
00:42:25,292 --> 00:42:26,544
-Come here.
-It's done.

626
00:42:26,627 --> 00:42:28,629
Let's sit down and eat. Come on, everyone.

627
00:42:28,712 --> 00:42:29,797
Come on. Let's eat.

628
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:31,423
-Fill your glasses.
-Fill them.

629
00:42:31,507 --> 00:42:33,467
-We should drink together.
-Fill them.

630
00:42:33,551 --> 00:42:34,385
Come here.

631
00:42:34,468 --> 00:42:36,011
You're too loud.

632
00:42:36,095 --> 00:42:38,347
-Thank you.
-Don't mention it.

633
00:42:38,430 --> 00:42:39,974
-Fill your glasses.
-Fill them.

634
00:42:40,057 --> 00:42:41,392
-Glasses up.
-Up!

635
00:42:41,475 --> 00:42:43,894
All right. Glasses up!

636
00:42:43,978 --> 00:42:45,563
Here's to Yeom Min-kyu!

637
00:42:45,646 --> 00:42:46,939
Cheers!

638
00:42:47,022 --> 00:42:49,191
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

639
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:51,527
Thank you.

640
00:42:58,075 --> 00:43:00,703
Mr. Ji, you worked so hard today.

641
00:43:00,786 --> 00:43:03,372
Not at all. Everyone else worked harder.

642
00:43:03,455 --> 00:43:05,666
Mr. Ji, eat up.

643
00:43:05,749 --> 00:43:07,126
Thank you.

644
00:43:07,209 --> 00:43:09,461
You don't have to do this.
I can help myself.

645
00:43:13,549 --> 00:43:14,383
Ms. Na.

646
00:43:14,466 --> 00:43:16,594
You should take off your gloves
and dig in.

647
00:43:22,725 --> 00:43:25,436
Wow, you two must be really close.

648
00:43:25,519 --> 00:43:26,812
I hear you go way back.

649
00:43:26,895 --> 00:43:29,940
Yeah. Those two are tight!

650
00:43:30,024 --> 00:43:32,151
Yes, we are pretty tight.

651
00:43:33,027 --> 00:43:35,029
She means the world to me.

652
00:43:49,043 --> 00:43:50,502
He can be kind of confusing.

653
00:43:50,586 --> 00:43:53,047
He's dangerously charming.

654
00:43:53,130 --> 00:43:55,132
Always making people get the wrong idea.

655
00:43:55,883 --> 00:43:57,468
Weird way to say you're a fan.

656
00:43:58,052 --> 00:44:00,387
So you aren't actually dating?

657
00:44:00,471 --> 00:44:01,722
You two look great together.

658
00:44:02,514 --> 00:44:03,474
Really?

659
00:44:04,475 --> 00:44:06,310
Ms. Na, she says we look great together.

660
00:44:07,561 --> 00:44:09,730
How could I date Eun-ho?

661
00:44:09,813 --> 00:44:14,318
Is Ms. Na going to make
the entertainment headlines

662
00:44:14,401 --> 00:44:16,695
before her miniseries even debuts?

663
00:44:16,779 --> 00:44:18,864
As "Ji Eun-ho's girl."

664
00:44:18,947 --> 00:44:20,032
Eun-ho's girl!

665
00:44:22,493 --> 00:44:23,952
That's enough. You're drunk.

666
00:44:28,582 --> 00:44:31,418
I can't listen to this anymore.
I'm getting uncomfortable.

667
00:44:31,919 --> 00:44:33,545
This is the problem with our society.

668
00:44:34,338 --> 00:44:37,925
When we see a man and a woman
who are close or around the same age,

669
00:44:38,008 --> 00:44:41,637
we always try to set them up
and push them to date.

670
00:44:42,429 --> 00:44:46,725
It's nothing more than entertainment
for thoughtless bystanders!

671
00:44:50,437 --> 00:44:52,981
Isn't it about time we stopped this?

672
00:44:53,607 --> 00:44:55,275
Just a fan!

673
00:44:56,819 --> 00:44:57,861
That's what she said.

674
00:44:58,612 --> 00:45:00,072
Mutual fans!

675
00:45:00,656 --> 00:45:01,573
Nothing more.

676
00:45:06,203 --> 00:45:08,080
Show some restraint.

677
00:45:08,163 --> 00:45:09,957
What's your problem?

678
00:45:10,833 --> 00:45:12,668
Did I do something wrong?

679
00:45:14,586 --> 00:45:16,588
Stop eating garlic, sir.

680
00:45:18,132 --> 00:45:19,299
What's with him?

681
00:45:23,178 --> 00:45:24,722
Did I do something wrong?

682
00:45:24,805 --> 00:45:27,975
People get on edge before something big.

683
00:45:28,058 --> 00:45:29,351
Something big?

684
00:45:29,852 --> 00:45:30,894
Is something going on?

685
00:45:32,813 --> 00:45:34,022
Oh.

686
00:45:34,523 --> 00:45:37,860
Actually, the chairwoman's
been pushing us to get married,

687
00:45:39,570 --> 00:45:41,613
so I think we'll be setting a date soon.

688
00:45:45,659 --> 00:45:48,704
You two are actually getting married?

689
00:45:48,787 --> 00:45:49,872
Ho-rang.

690
00:45:50,372 --> 00:45:51,540
Is it true?

691
00:45:52,291 --> 00:45:55,085
Why is everyone so surprised?
It already made the news.

692
00:45:56,378 --> 00:45:59,465
It's almost like you thought
we weren't going to get married.

693
00:45:59,548 --> 00:46:00,924
No. Not at all.

694
00:46:01,008 --> 00:46:04,386
My sincere congratulations.
Invite me to the wedding, okay?

695
00:46:04,470 --> 00:46:05,429
A get-together!

696
00:46:05,512 --> 00:46:07,890
-Ho-rang. A get-together!
-It's not happening--

697
00:46:11,685 --> 00:46:13,854
You said you needed three months.

698
00:46:14,480 --> 00:46:16,565
The three months aren't up yet.

699
00:46:19,026 --> 00:46:20,527
The chairwoman's backed off, hasn't she?

700
00:46:22,488 --> 00:46:25,240
I asked her to be patient a little longer.

701
00:46:28,368 --> 00:46:30,329
You should stay on my good side.

702
00:46:57,689 --> 00:47:00,400
Bo-bae, want to get some fresh air?

703
00:47:13,664 --> 00:47:14,957
We'll be right back.

704
00:47:21,630 --> 00:47:23,465
Bo-bae, are you okay?

705
00:47:23,549 --> 00:47:24,383
Yeah.

706
00:47:28,387 --> 00:47:29,221
Huh?

707
00:47:30,180 --> 00:47:32,015
My shoelace is untied.

708
00:47:32,099 --> 00:47:33,475
Bo-bae. Hold on.

709
00:47:35,644 --> 00:47:36,603
Sit here.

710
00:47:42,276 --> 00:47:44,695
You can't just touch me like that.

711
00:47:45,529 --> 00:47:48,073
I know. I'll tie it without touching you.

712
00:47:48,156 --> 00:47:51,785
What do you know? You might actually…

713
00:47:52,286 --> 00:47:55,163
I really do know, Bo-bae.
I know your condition.

714
00:47:56,832 --> 00:47:59,209
We've known each other for three years.

715
00:47:59,710 --> 00:48:00,919
How could I not know?

716
00:48:01,003 --> 00:48:03,380
If you knew, why did you…

717
00:48:05,424 --> 00:48:07,718
It seemed like you wanted to hide it.

718
00:48:11,722 --> 00:48:14,391
I didn't want someone I like to know
I knew their weakness.

719
00:48:20,480 --> 00:48:21,523
And

720
00:48:22,524 --> 00:48:25,861
I also know nothing happens
when you touch Mr. Baek.

721
00:48:28,572 --> 00:48:30,157
He's…

722
00:48:30,240 --> 00:48:32,200
I don't know why it doesn't affect him…

723
00:48:39,625 --> 00:48:40,876
but it doesn't matter now.

724
00:48:43,337 --> 00:48:44,212
Bo-bae.

725
00:48:48,175 --> 00:48:50,177
To you, am I really

726
00:48:51,345 --> 00:48:53,430
just a close friend

727
00:48:54,640 --> 00:48:56,016
and a good actor?

728
00:48:58,060 --> 00:48:59,186
That's it?

729
00:49:02,439 --> 00:49:03,273
Eun-ho.

730
00:49:03,357 --> 00:49:04,566
That's not how I feel.

731
00:49:05,525 --> 00:49:06,360
MBS DRAMA

732
00:49:06,443 --> 00:49:08,403
CEHONGDAM INTERNATIONAL UNIVERSITY
AUDITION

733
00:49:18,163 --> 00:49:21,041
"I just didn't know
how to comfort you, so…"

734
00:49:21,124 --> 00:49:23,752
"Earlier, I tried to comfort you,
but I just…"

735
00:49:23,835 --> 00:49:26,964
"Earlier, I tried to comfort you,
but I only made you uncomfortable."

736
00:49:29,049 --> 00:49:30,592
"I just didn't know how to…"

737
00:49:30,676 --> 00:49:32,260
"They say…"

738
00:49:32,344 --> 00:49:33,387
"Earlier…"

739
00:49:34,012 --> 00:49:36,598
"…the darkest hour is just before dawn."

740
00:49:37,099 --> 00:49:41,019
"They say the darkest hour
is just before dawn."

741
00:49:41,603 --> 00:49:43,313
"There's a saying…"

742
00:49:46,108 --> 00:49:47,109
Dark…

743
00:49:50,112 --> 00:49:52,155
"Don't give up…"

744
00:49:54,282 --> 00:49:55,659
BLACK PARTNER
AUDITION

745
00:50:24,646 --> 00:50:27,190
-Hello!
-Oh, the male lead is here.

746
00:50:27,274 --> 00:50:29,151
Everyone, let's give him a big hand!

747
00:50:39,077 --> 00:50:39,911
He's so handsome!

748
00:50:40,912 --> 00:50:43,623
Eun-ho, meet our writer.

749
00:50:48,170 --> 00:50:50,839
-Hello, Ms. Writer.
-Hello.

750
00:50:51,465 --> 00:50:52,674
So you're the writer.

751
00:50:57,554 --> 00:50:58,805
You are the one

752
00:50:59,514 --> 00:51:01,433
who makes my heart race.

753
00:51:06,772 --> 00:51:09,149
Can't you see me that way too?

754
00:51:11,651 --> 00:51:12,486
That's…

755
00:51:13,070 --> 00:51:16,615
Hey, everyone's heart races.

756
00:51:17,115 --> 00:51:19,701
And let's say I return your feelings.

757
00:51:19,785 --> 00:51:24,247
You might never be able to hold my hand
or kiss me for the rest of your life.

758
00:51:24,331 --> 00:51:25,582
You'd be okay with that?

759
00:51:26,541 --> 00:51:28,668
I waited three years for the right moment.

760
00:51:29,169 --> 00:51:31,505
"When I'm a better actor."

761
00:51:31,588 --> 00:51:33,048
"When I'm more successful."

762
00:51:35,675 --> 00:51:38,470
But I realized there's no perfect time.

763
00:51:39,805 --> 00:51:40,764
Eun-ho.

764
00:51:45,102 --> 00:51:46,144
I like you.

765
00:51:50,232 --> 00:51:51,775
Can't this be enough?

766
00:52:36,236 --> 00:52:39,197
It's obvious this is an important moment.
Let's not interrupt.

767
00:52:41,074 --> 00:52:42,367
Let go.

768
00:52:45,287 --> 00:52:46,621
Do you like Ms. Na Bo-bae?

769
00:52:51,960 --> 00:52:56,131
I don't see why I should answer that.

770
00:52:56,214 --> 00:52:57,924
You really don't?

771
00:52:58,008 --> 00:53:00,051
Are you threatening me?

772
00:53:01,011 --> 00:53:02,762
No, I'm just telling the truth.

773
00:53:03,513 --> 00:53:05,682
Whether we get married or not,

774
00:53:05,765 --> 00:53:08,101
I'm the one cutting you some slack
for the next three months.

775
00:53:08,185 --> 00:53:10,729
I asked for time to prove myself,

776
00:53:10,812 --> 00:53:12,939
not for you to push me around.

777
00:53:14,191 --> 00:53:15,150
Also…

778
00:53:20,238 --> 00:53:21,823
you asked me if I liked her.

779
00:53:23,658 --> 00:53:26,036
If I said I like her,

780
00:53:26,745 --> 00:53:28,205
would you call off the wedding?

781
00:53:31,958 --> 00:53:35,503
In all my plans from A to Z,

782
00:53:35,587 --> 00:53:39,549
there isn't a single outcome
where I don't take over TS.

783
00:53:40,592 --> 00:53:44,429
I'll put TS back on top of the industry,
no matter what.

784
00:53:44,512 --> 00:53:46,681
But if you think about it,

785
00:53:46,765 --> 00:53:51,228
the fact that you have so many plans
means you're not certain.

786
00:53:52,604 --> 00:53:54,272
Anyway, I'll wait for you.

787
00:53:54,356 --> 00:53:57,234
I'm curious to see
what you're capable of, Mr. Baek.

788
00:54:22,550 --> 00:54:23,718
Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

789
00:54:27,806 --> 00:54:30,517
Where have you been all this time?

790
00:54:31,893 --> 00:54:36,022
I just went for a walk to sober up.

791
00:54:37,190 --> 00:54:39,317
What are you doing here?

792
00:54:39,818 --> 00:54:44,322
Earlier, after announcing your wedding,
you were whispering with Ms. Han.

793
00:54:50,203 --> 00:54:51,037
Well…

794
00:54:52,372 --> 00:54:53,623
Does it bother you?

795
00:54:55,875 --> 00:54:57,168
No.

796
00:55:05,885 --> 00:55:06,845
"Still,

797
00:55:07,512 --> 00:55:09,055
let's keep going."

798
00:55:11,766 --> 00:55:13,643
Where did that come from?

799
00:55:17,272 --> 00:55:22,360
"Even if the whole world
feels like an enemy and a burden,

800
00:55:23,820 --> 00:55:26,281
and nothing works
no matter how hard you try,

801
00:55:26,364 --> 00:55:28,241
try again."

802
00:55:29,284 --> 00:55:32,370
"Even through tears, don't give up."

803
00:55:33,288 --> 00:55:34,289
"For now…

804
00:55:36,291 --> 00:55:37,292
let's just…

805
00:55:40,378 --> 00:55:42,297
keep going."

806
00:55:47,844 --> 00:55:50,221
You watched Wistful Youth?

807
00:55:53,600 --> 00:55:55,602
You kept talking about it, so…

808
00:55:57,395 --> 00:55:58,563
To you,

809
00:55:58,646 --> 00:56:03,193
it may be just another one-hour drama
no one knows about,

810
00:56:03,276 --> 00:56:06,988
but it means the world to me.

811
00:56:08,281 --> 00:56:09,407
Still,

812
00:56:11,242 --> 00:56:12,869
let's keep going.

813
00:56:13,578 --> 00:56:16,122
Even if the whole world
feels like an enemy and a burden,

814
00:56:16,623 --> 00:56:19,793
and nothing works
no matter how hard you try,

815
00:56:19,876 --> 00:56:21,127
try again.

816
00:56:22,462 --> 00:56:24,255
Even through tears, don't give up.

817
00:56:26,007 --> 00:56:29,386
For now, let's just keep going.

818
00:56:53,451 --> 00:56:58,289
Well, I can see why you and Mr. Ji Eun-ho
have such a special relationship.

819
00:56:58,373 --> 00:57:01,626
If I acted in a script like that,

820
00:57:02,335 --> 00:57:04,587
I'd become a fan of the writer too.

821
00:57:10,760 --> 00:57:11,719
You know,

822
00:57:12,804 --> 00:57:13,763
I'm also…

823
00:57:20,270 --> 00:57:21,396
a fan of yours…

824
00:57:23,398 --> 00:57:24,691
Ms. Na.

825
00:57:27,277 --> 00:57:28,570
There you go again.

826
00:57:29,362 --> 00:57:31,823
It's okay. No need to say nice things.

827
00:57:31,906 --> 00:57:33,158
I want to…

828
00:57:35,368 --> 00:57:36,369
keep going

829
00:57:38,163 --> 00:57:39,664
with you.

830
00:57:41,875 --> 00:57:42,876
For now,

831
00:57:43,960 --> 00:57:45,003
let's just

832
00:57:46,087 --> 00:57:47,172
keep going.

833
00:57:51,176 --> 00:57:52,218
Wherever it takes us.

834
00:58:01,644 --> 00:58:02,729
It's me.

835
00:58:04,230 --> 00:58:05,857
Did you get a good shot earlier?

836
00:58:09,986 --> 00:58:13,907
Edit the video
to get Ji Eun-ho's fans riled up.

837
00:58:14,991 --> 00:58:16,743
Make it really trashy…

838
00:58:18,995 --> 00:58:20,205
and entertaining.

839
00:58:21,664 --> 00:58:23,875
Is this for real? My gosh.

840
00:58:23,958 --> 00:58:26,002
-Crazy, right?
-This is insane.

841
00:58:26,628 --> 00:58:29,130
-Good morning. Did you all sleep well?
-My gosh.

842
00:58:32,842 --> 00:58:35,929
Impressive. Truly impressive.

843
00:58:36,596 --> 00:58:40,183
I told you.
I saw her doing it with Mr. Baek too.

844
00:58:41,309 --> 00:58:42,936
How did she even get to Eun-ho?

845
00:58:50,109 --> 00:58:51,236
Yes, Ms. Chu.

846
00:58:55,532 --> 00:58:56,366
Sorry?

847
00:58:56,991 --> 00:59:00,119
The shocking identity
of the woman Ji Eun-ho proposed to.

848
00:59:00,203 --> 00:59:04,165
A video of Ji Eun-ho proposing was leaked,
sending all of Korea into a frenzy.

849
00:59:04,249 --> 00:59:07,669
It turns out the woman in the video
is a drama writer.

850
00:59:07,752 --> 00:59:10,630
She wrote the one-ep drama
that gave Ji Eun-ho his first lead role,

851
00:59:10,713 --> 00:59:12,257
then dropped off the radar.

852
00:59:12,340 --> 00:59:15,218
There's been a lot of buzz
about her new drama,

853
00:59:15,301 --> 00:59:17,762
but turns out she got it
by flirting with Ji Eun-ho.

854
00:59:18,346 --> 00:59:21,015
A real drama writer
should let her script do the talking.

855
00:59:23,184 --> 00:59:25,019
SHE WROTE JI EUN-HO'S FIRST LEAD DRAMA

856
00:59:25,103 --> 00:59:26,771
TRYING TO BAG A CELEB AND LEVEL UP

857
00:59:26,854 --> 00:59:28,106
Man, this is…

858
00:59:28,189 --> 00:59:29,941
Damn.

859
00:59:30,024 --> 00:59:31,484
It's only been up for a bit,

860
00:59:31,568 --> 00:59:34,404
but there are already many videos
with the same comments.

861
00:59:35,488 --> 00:59:37,699
This isn't one person. It's coordinated.

862
00:59:39,158 --> 00:59:41,786
I'll get all the details as fast as I can.

863
00:59:41,869 --> 00:59:43,496
We should get back to Seoul.

864
00:59:43,580 --> 00:59:46,708
If fans swarm the airport,
it'll be a nightmare.

865
00:59:46,791 --> 00:59:49,294
We should all head to the airport
separately.

866
01:00:20,241 --> 01:00:21,784
This isn't good.

867
01:00:22,619 --> 01:00:24,662
We probably shouldn't move as a group.

868
01:00:24,746 --> 01:00:25,788
We should split up.

869
01:00:25,872 --> 01:00:27,665
-Seo-jeong, bring the luggage.
-Sorry?

870
01:00:28,249 --> 01:00:30,209
Grab the luggage. Follow me!

871
01:00:31,544 --> 01:00:32,378
Seo-jeong!

872
01:00:32,462 --> 01:00:33,463
Hide well. Okay?

873
01:00:50,563 --> 01:00:51,648
Isn't she that writer?

874
01:00:51,731 --> 01:00:53,232
-Let me see.
-What?

875
01:00:53,316 --> 01:00:54,400
It's her.

876
01:00:54,484 --> 01:00:55,318
It's that woman!

877
01:00:55,401 --> 01:00:57,362
-Follow me.
-Damn, she's all covered up.

878
01:00:57,445 --> 01:00:59,739
-It's her.
-It's that woman.

879
01:01:06,454 --> 01:01:08,331
-It's her.
-It's that woman.

880
01:01:08,414 --> 01:01:10,124
Damn, she's all covered up.

881
01:01:10,208 --> 01:01:12,919
-Leave our Eun-ho alone!
-You crazy bitch!

882
01:01:27,100 --> 01:01:28,685
I need to hold it in.

883
01:01:30,103 --> 01:01:31,396
I have to hold it in.

884
01:01:32,689 --> 01:01:34,399
No, Na Bo-bae.

885
01:01:34,482 --> 01:01:36,734
Hold it in. If you can't hold it in here…

886
01:04:53,681 --> 01:04:58,311
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
